    "text": "To determine the combined number of degrees that Summer and Jolly have, we start by defining the number of degrees Jolly has as \\( x \\). According to the problem, Summer has five more degrees than Jolly, and Summer has a total of 150 degrees. Therefore, we can express the number of degrees Summer has as \\( x + 5 \\).\n\nWe know that Summer has 150 degrees, so we can set up the following equation:\n\\[ x + 5 = 150 \\]\n\nTo find the value of \\( x \\), we subtract 5 from both sides of the equation:\n\\[ x = 150 - 5 \\]\n\\[ x = 145 \\]\n\nSo, Jolly has 145 degrees. The combined number of degrees that Summer and Jolly have is the sum of their degrees:\n\\[ 150 + 145 = 295 \\]\n\nThus, the combined number of degrees they both have is \\(\\boxed{295}\\).",
